ao_coreaudio: wait for the mixability too when changing the physical format

ca_change_physical_format_sync() waits until the stream's physical format
equals the requested one, using ca_asbd_equals(), which ignores
kAudioFormatFlagIsNonMixable. On macOS 27 (2026-11-05, Jabra Link 380 USB
headset, mpv master 9028187538 and dc4b285c93 alike) the device applies the
sample format at once and the mixability ~300 ms later. So the exclusive
output's "switch to non-mixable s16" returned at once with the format still
mixable. init then read a float virtual format, and the late flip to
non-mixable fired property_listener_cb ("Stream format changed!
Reloading."). The reload's restore to the original mixable format did the
same in the other direction. Result: 10 exclusive opens in 7 s, then
"can't start audio device ([35]...)", and the device was unusable for
shared output until coreaudiod restarted.

Compare the mixability as well. If the device never applies it, the
existing 2 s timeout ends the wait and the format counts as set (the
sample format is what was asked for), rather than being reverted.

Not upstream yet. Drop this patch once mpv waits for the mixability itself.

--- a/audio/out/ao_coreaudio_utils.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_coreaudio_utils.c
@@ -510,12 +510,21 @@
         if (!CHECK_CA_WARN("could not retrieve physical format"))
             break;
 
+        // ca_asbd_equals() ignores kAudioFormatFlagIsNonMixable. On macOS 27
+        // a device can apply the sample format at once and the mixability
+        // ~300 ms later, so without this the wait returns before the change
+        // has landed and the late update reads as an outside format change.
         format_set = ca_asbd_equals(&change_format, &actual_format);
-        if (format_set)
+        if (format_set &&
+            (change_format.mFormatFlags & kAudioFormatFlagIsNonMixable) ==
+            (actual_format.mFormatFlags & kAudioFormatFlagIsNonMixable))
             break;
 
         if (mp_cond_timedwait_until(&sem->cond, &sem->mutex, wait_until)) {
-            MP_VERBOSE(ao, "reached timeout\n");
+            // A device that never applies the mixability still has the
+            // format we asked for: keep it rather than restoring the old one.
+            MP_VERBOSE(ao, "reached timeout%s\n",
+                       format_set ? " (mixability never changed)" : "");
             break;
         }
     }
